cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "love-in-translation: a falsification-first evidence review and formal model of how care moves between people"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-04
authors:
  - family-names: Poulain
    given-names: Julien
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/julienaxyomlabs/love-in-translation"
abstract: >-
  Tests the hypothesis that love intended, expressed, perceived and received
  diverge, and that relationship problems stem from the translation of care
  rather than its amount. The repository contains a 22-chapter evidence review
  with graded claims and Crossref-verified citations, a formal model of dyadic
  care transmission, and a standard-library Python implementation whose tests
  execute the model's mathematical claims.
keywords:
  - relationship science
  - perceived partner responsiveness
  - social support
  - dyadic data analysis
  - response surface analysis
  - signal detection
  - Bayesian inference
  - family psychology
  - Korea
